A||||3||rogergarrison||Engine Compartment Lite||||3||
Z||000000||rogergarrison||02-06-2001||07:30 AM||||For some lite in the engine compt for those nightime emergencies. I found a late model GM pickup truck in the junkyard. In the engine compartment on the passenger side fenderwell theres a little lite on a bracket screwed to it. it has about 10' of coiled wire and hooked to battery. You can just pop it out of the bracket and flip the little switch on the side to get lite anywhere around the car, interior, engine, change a flat. Only cost me $5.00. i just screwed it inside the end of my rear trunk. when your done just wind the little crank to wind up the wire and pop it back in clip.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Oreif||02-06-2001||10:16 AM||||That sounds like an excellent idea! I'll have to grab a few so I can put them on my other vehicles too. Thanks for the tip.||||reg||14
Z||000002||stsmithgt||02-06-2001||10:25 AM||||My brother has a Chevy truck with one of those lights.  That is a very usefull tool.  It saved me from having to dig up a flash light several times.  It's been low on my priority list, but I'll get one of those lights in the compartment one of these days.  Have you noticed, not many Chevy trucks to pick from at the auto wreckers.  Might have to go to a Truck only wrecker.  ||||reg||14
Z||000003||TheFiero64||02-06-2001||02:22 PM||||Here is a pic I took at the kickhill swap meet of a light install.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1249362&a=9233500&p=30056750&Sequence=0&res=high"> <P><BR>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 02-06-2001).]||||reg||10
